# Distinct supplied-evidence variants avoid duplicating adjacent explanation cards.
add('10-033','Describe what follows from these observations: solution X contains an OH-bearing organic molecule but is neutral; solution Y contains sodium hydroxide and is alkaline. Can the letters OH alone establish alkalinity?','No: X is a counterexample. In Y hydroxide ions account for alkalinity; OH written within a molecular formula need not represent free hydroxide ions.','Neutral X disproves the proposed OH-letter rule (1).|Distinguish molecular OH from the hydroxide ions in Y (1).',ao=['B'],subtype='INTERP',bloom='Analyse')
add('10-040','Describe how to distinguish the functional groups in CH3CH2OH and CH3C(=O)OH by tracing the carbon attached to oxygen.','In CH3CH2OH the OH-bearing carbon has no C=O bond, giving an alcohol. In CH3C(=O)OH the OH is attached to a carbonyl carbon, giving a carboxylic acid.','First displayed connectivity identifies an alcohol group (1).|Second connectivity identifies the complete carboxyl group (1).',ao=['B'],subtype='INTERP',bloom='Analyse')
add('10-062','Describe which evidence supports identifying fibre X as protein rather than nylon: both fibres contain amide links, but hydrolysis of X produces amino acids and hydrolysis of Y produces a diamine and a dicarboxylic acid.','The amino-acid products support protein for X. The shared amide links alone do not distinguish X from Y; Y’s different products support a different polyamide.','Link X’s amino-acid products to protein building units (1).|Explain why shared amide links alone cannot distinguish the fibres (1).',ao=['B'],subtype='INTERP',bloom='Analyse')
add('10-080','Describe the limitation of a waste-treatment trial that reports a plastic bag disappeared from sight after shredding but measures neither polymer breakdown nor the resulting fragments.','Loss of visibility establishes fragmentation, not chemical biodegradation. Without collecting or tracking the fragments the trial cannot show removal of persistent plastic from the environment.','Visual disappearance does not demonstrate chemical breakdown (1).|Missing fragment tracking prevents a claim of environmental removal (1).',ao=['B'],subtype='APP',bloom='Analyse')
add('11-020','Describe why a farmer might apply nitrogen- and phosphorus-containing fertilisers.','Nitrogen replaces a deficient nutrient needed for amino acids and proteins; phosphorus replaces a nutrient needed for processes including root development.','Nitrogen supply linked to protein production and growth (1).|Phosphorus supply linked to root development (1).',ao=['A'],subtype='FEATURE',bloom='Remember',recall=2)
